WEBVTT

00:00.650 --> 00:03.280
<i>It's the finals of the Shizuoka Prefecture Tournament.</i>

00:03.280 --> 00:06.230
<i>The opponent is the famous Shimizu FC.</i>

00:06.230 --> 00:09.980
<i>Right as the match starts, Tsubasa is completely marked</i>

00:09.980 --> 00:12.320
<i>and can't move freely.</i>

00:12.320 --> 00:15.660
<i>To make things worse, opponents' players aimed for Wakabayashi,</i>

00:15.660 --> 00:17.740
<i>ramming into him on purpose to stop him.</i>

00:18.310 --> 00:22.080
<i>The injury in his leg flared up, leaving Wakabayashi unable to move normally.</i>

00:22.080 --> 00:28.080
<i>However, his tenacity to protect the goal got through to Tsubasa.</i>

00:28.080 --> 00:31.920
<i>He managed to break through a 3-man marking, scoring a goal.</i>

00:32.670 --> 00:36.130
<i>Nankatsu FC won the Shizuoka Prefecture Tournament,</i>

00:36.130 --> 00:40.510
<i>and won a ticket to the National Tournament.</i>

00:41.640 --> 00:43.680
Hey, Tsubasa! Stop snatching food!

00:43.680 --> 00:44.630
Ouch!

00:44.630 --> 00:49.100
Breakfast is almost ready, so go and take a shower.

00:49.100 --> 00:50.900
But mom, I'm starving!

00:50.900 --> 00:52.020
Can't you hurry up?

00:52.020 --> 00:53.160
Don't talk back to me!

00:53.160 --> 00:55.400
<i>This is an ordinary morning at the Ozoras'.</i>

00:55.820 --> 00:58.680
<i>Captain, Mrs. Ozora, Tsubasa...</i>

00:58.680 --> 01:02.450
<i>The Ozora Family is plenty happy as they are now.</i>

01:02.450 --> 01:05.930
<i>But, even though it's what all of them want...</i>

01:05.930 --> 01:08.960
<i>Is it really okay for me to take Tsubasa with me to Brazil...?</i>

01:09.390 --> 01:11.770
<i>A family is meant to be together...</i>

01:11.770 --> 01:15.960
<i>Wouldn't I just shatter their happiness...?</i>

01:15.960 --> 01:17.590
Roberto!

01:18.620 --> 01:19.840
What's wrong?

01:19.840 --> 01:22.120
It's nothing.

01:22.120 --> 01:23.600
Is that so?

01:39.020 --> 01:44.650
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:39.020 --> 01:44.650
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:44.650 --> 01:49.650
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:44.650 --> 01:49.650
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:50.320 --> 01:55.490
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:50.320 --> 01:55.490
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:56.200 --> 02:03.850
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:56.200 --> 02:03.850
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

02:03.850 --> 02:09.590
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

02:03.850 --> 02:09.590
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

02:09.590 --> 02:18.100
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

02:09.590 --> 02:18.100
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

02:18.100 --> 02:23.900
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

02:18.100 --> 02:23.900
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

02:23.900 --> 02:29.820
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

02:23.900 --> 02:29.820
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:29.820 --> 02:31.320
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:31.320 --> 02:38.620
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:31.320 --> 02:38.620
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:38.620 --> 02:41.540
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

02:38.620 --> 02:41.540
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

02:41.540 --> 02:46.460
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

02:41.540 --> 02:46.460
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:57.070 --> 03:00.240
<b><b>EPISODE 13:
AND THEN, THE NATIONALS</b></b>

03:00.580 --> 03:03.030
THE 6TH NATIONAL YOUTH FOOTBALL TOURNAMENT

03:00.580 --> 03:03.030
HOKKAIDO TOURNAMENT FINAL

03:04.580 --> 03:06.720
The hell are you doing, Sapporo FC?

03:06.720 --> 03:08.040
Hurry up and get that ball!

03:08.040 --> 03:10.040
There's only one minute left!

03:10.780 --> 03:11.600
Captain!

03:11.600 --> 03:15.640
<i>Sapporo FC is unable to steal the ball, despite the desperate attempts of many players!</i>

03:15.640 --> 03:18.340
<i>Matsuyama, Furano's captain, shows off his smooth ball-keeping!</i>

03:18.640 --> 03:20.050
<i>Like I'd let you have the ball!</i>

03:21.050 --> 03:21.760
Damn it!

03:25.040 --> 03:27.760
He's so persistent! Hurry up and take it away!

03:27.760 --> 03:29.120
Captain, pass it!

03:29.120 --> 03:32.810
There's no way. He's completely surrounded! He can't get a pass out!

03:32.810 --> 03:36.310
<i>Matsuyama continues to hold the ball in a narrow spot.</i>

03:36.310 --> 03:38.820
<i>Will he be able to keep it away from his opponents?</i>

03:38.820 --> 03:41.490
<i>We've gone into stoppage time!</i>

03:41.490 --> 03:45.450
Will Sapporo FC, the prefectural tournament favorite, really lose?

03:45.450 --> 03:48.620
Come on, Furano! Hang on for just a little longer!

03:49.010 --> 03:51.190
Captain, please do your best!

03:55.170 --> 03:57.840
<i>It's the referee's whistle!</i>

03:58.250 --> 04:01.310
We did it!

04:01.310 --> 04:03.000
<i>An absolutely stunning upset!</i>

04:03.000 --> 04:06.300
<i>Everyone's favorite for victory, Sapporo FC, is defeated!</i>

04:07.080 --> 04:09.850
<i>Furano Elementary Football Club will be participating in the Nationals for the first time,</i>

04:09.850 --> 04:11.240
<i>finally realizing a long-awaited dream!</i>

04:11.240 --> 04:13.060
<i>Furano Elementary Football Club is a team with barely</i>

04:13.060 --> 04:16.630
<i>11 members, including their captain, Matsuyama, and have practiced hard.</i>

04:16.630 --> 04:20.190
<i>This victory was won through that hard work!</i>

04:20.840 --> 04:24.340
We did well to fill up the hole Misaki left behind.

04:24.340 --> 04:25.540
Yes.

04:25.540 --> 04:28.180
We'll see him in the Nationals next.

04:28.180 --> 04:29.200
Yes.

04:29.990 --> 04:32.080
<i>Misaki, we've won!</i>

04:32.080 --> 04:35.040
<i>I want to play against you in the National Tournament.</i>

04:46.270 --> 04:48.760
So you've finished your painting, dad.

04:48.760 --> 04:50.600
Will we be moving again?

04:51.130 --> 04:52.220
Yes.

04:53.770 --> 04:56.110
When the Nationals are over,

04:56.110 --> 04:58.770
you'll be going to a different school for the second semester.

04:58.770 --> 05:01.240
Make sure to let your friends know.

05:01.240 --> 05:02.530
Yeah!

05:09.160 --> 05:12.390
In the end, it'd be better to give up on the idea of going to Nationals.

05:12.390 --> 05:13.210
I won't!

05:13.210 --> 05:14.500
Calm down, Genzo.

05:14.500 --> 05:17.440
Your body is still developing.

05:17.440 --> 05:18.730
You shouldn't push yourself too hard.

05:18.730 --> 05:22.910
It's obvious that your leg will get worse if you go out and play.

05:22.910 --> 05:26.230
Please, bear with it until your leg is fully healed.

05:26.230 --> 05:27.620
He's right, Genzo.

05:27.620 --> 05:31.010
There's always next time for you. Just give up this once.

05:31.600 --> 05:36.770
There's still someone I need to pay back, no matter what.

05:38.520 --> 05:41.610
<i>I'm sorry, the young master is currently not at home.</i>

05:41.610 --> 05:44.200
It's no use, she says captain is not home.

05:44.200 --> 05:47.190
Does that mean that his leg is fine now?

05:47.190 --> 05:48.570
I hope it is.

05:48.570 --> 05:53.310
I want him to heal soon so that we can play in the Nationals together.

05:53.310 --> 05:56.180
Then, we'll bring the championship pennant back home with us once more.

05:56.180 --> 05:57.460
Yeah!

05:58.270 --> 05:59.330
Come on, Ryo!

05:59.330 --> 06:00.290
Clean the floor properly!

06:00.290 --> 06:02.710
Can't you just leave me alone?

06:02.710 --> 06:06.170
I don't work here, you know!

06:06.170 --> 06:08.560
Look who's talking.

06:08.560 --> 06:12.890
Your team won the tournament, but they didn't even let you play once.

06:12.890 --> 06:14.890
What can I do about that?

06:14.890 --> 06:17.530
Everyone we have on the team is great.

06:17.530 --> 06:19.980
And that's precisely why you should clean the tiles like this!

06:19.980 --> 06:21.840
Give those legs a good workout!

06:22.600 --> 06:25.570
Just when I thought I had a day off...

06:28.330 --> 06:34.660
<i>And that's how the Nankatsu Eleven spent their time on the break before Nationals.</i>

06:34.980 --> 06:36.990
<i>As for Tsubasa...</i>

06:47.760 --> 06:49.050
What's wrong with you, Tsubasa?

06:49.050 --> 06:51.700
Is a ball like this so difficult?

06:51.700 --> 06:53.220
Yeah...

06:55.180 --> 06:58.070
<i>I wonder what's wrong with Roberto today.</i>

06:58.070 --> 07:00.350
<i>He's different from usual.</i>

07:02.890 --> 07:06.240
Tsubasa, are you really sure about going to Brazil?

07:06.240 --> 07:09.190
Of course! What's all this about?

07:09.190 --> 07:14.250
If you go to Brazil, your mom will be left alone, you know.

07:14.250 --> 07:16.880
Are you really willing to go to Brazil with me?

07:16.880 --> 07:17.910
What?

07:17.910 --> 07:21.870
Roberto, I really do want to go to Brazil.

07:23.420 --> 07:25.380
It's just... I have started thinking that

07:25.380 --> 07:30.630
I might be forcing my dream on you.

07:30.630 --> 07:33.720
That I might be tearing your family apart.

07:33.720 --> 07:36.370
Roberto, but I—

07:36.370 --> 07:38.180
Tsubasa, this is—

07:40.110 --> 07:41.730
Wakabayashi!

07:41.730 --> 07:44.350
Tsubasa, we need to talk.

07:46.780 --> 07:49.860
I can't go to the National Tournament.

07:49.860 --> 07:50.860
What?

07:52.050 --> 07:55.960
It looks like my injury is worse than I thought.

07:55.960 --> 07:57.900
I need to stay to get it treated.

07:58.780 --> 08:02.250
So Tsubasa, I need a favor from you.

08:02.800 --> 08:07.220
Even if I'm not there, I want to you to keep winning

08:07.220 --> 08:09.580
until you play against Kojiro Hyuga's Meiwa FC.

08:09.580 --> 08:10.920
Wakabayashi...

08:11.370 --> 08:16.230
I really need to pay him back for the time he scored that goal on me.

08:16.230 --> 08:19.380
I'll make sure my leg is fully healed for that match against Meiwa.

08:19.380 --> 08:22.560
So, Tsubasa... I'm counting on you!

08:23.370 --> 08:26.400
Got it. I'll just focus on winning until then!

08:31.680 --> 08:32.190
Go, go!

08:34.700 --> 08:35.650
Over here!

08:37.720 --> 08:40.500
What's wrong with you, guys? I can't hear you!

08:40.500 --> 08:42.470
If this much of heat makes you give up,

08:42.470 --> 08:45.000
you can't possibly win the National Tournament!

08:45.000 --> 08:45.620
Yes!

08:46.660 --> 08:49.680
Do you think Wakabayashi's absence

08:49.680 --> 08:52.210
is weighing on the boys' minds?

08:52.210 --> 08:53.180
Yes.

08:53.180 --> 08:58.310
They feel the impact of Wakabayashi's absence on the team's strength

08:58.310 --> 08:59.760
more than we do.

08:59.760 --> 09:03.320
Moreover, in addition to being the pillar of our defense,

09:03.320 --> 09:05.770
Wakabayashi kept the whole team together as the captain.

09:05.770 --> 09:10.130
Games aside, the fact that they can't go to Tokyo with him

09:10.130 --> 09:12.440
will further impact the team's morale.

09:12.440 --> 09:16.260
Despite all of that, the people who are still full of energy are Tsubasa...

09:16.260 --> 09:17.280
Misaki!

09:17.280 --> 09:18.960
Take that! One, two!

09:18.960 --> 09:20.960
... and Misaki, who always does things his own way.

09:23.710 --> 09:25.540
I did it!

09:25.540 --> 09:28.650
You dumbass! Can't you even stop that?

09:28.650 --> 09:32.750
When Wakabayashi isn't around, you're the only one we can count on!

09:30.550 --> 09:32.750
You can add Ishizaki there too.

09:35.630 --> 09:40.140
<i>I made a promise to Wakabayashi that I'll keep winning!</i>

09:45.730 --> 09:47.230
Mrs. Ozora!

09:47.230 --> 09:51.230
Won't you be lonely if Tsubasa leaves, living by yourself?

09:51.230 --> 09:54.100
What? Why the sudden question?

09:54.100 --> 09:55.820
Please tell me, Mrs. Ozora.

09:58.520 --> 10:02.320
Well, I'd be lying if I said that I wouldn't feel lonely,

10:02.320 --> 10:07.590
but as my husband says, a parent can't be an obstacle to their child's dream.

10:07.590 --> 10:10.330
But Tsubasa is still in elementary school!

10:10.330 --> 10:15.060
Well, Tsubasa is surprisingly level-headed for his age.

10:15.060 --> 10:18.840
He really wants to be a first-class football player,

10:18.840 --> 10:21.340
and that's Tsubasa's dream.

10:21.340 --> 10:27.020
So, I really think he was besides himself when you asked him to go with you.

10:27.020 --> 10:30.360
If he puts his heart and soul into realizing his dream

10:30.360 --> 10:33.990
and charges ahead without looking back,

10:33.990 --> 10:36.190
I'll be happy too.

10:37.580 --> 10:39.450
You did well, guys.

10:39.450 --> 10:41.250
In three days, we'll finally be heading off

10:41.250 --> 10:44.370
to participate in the National Tournament in Tokyo.

10:44.370 --> 10:47.700
So, I'll be appointing a new captain.

10:47.700 --> 10:48.890
A new captain?

10:48.890 --> 10:50.040
What about Wakabayashi?

10:50.040 --> 10:54.090
Unfortunately, he's unable to participate in the National Tournament, as his injury has worsened.

10:54.090 --> 10:58.840
That's why we need someone to fill Wakabayashi's role here.

10:58.840 --> 11:01.590
It's true that his absence is a hard blow for us.

11:01.590 --> 11:06.930
However, if we just get hung up on that, we won't be able to move forward.

11:07.500 --> 11:08.850
So, I'll be announcing it now.

11:09.680 --> 11:12.480
The new captain of Nankatsu FC is...

11:15.120 --> 11:17.300
Tsubasa Ozora!

11:17.300 --> 11:19.240
Me?

11:19.240 --> 11:20.900
You did it, Tsubasa!

11:20.900 --> 11:22.290
So, it's Tsubasa.

11:22.290 --> 11:24.490
It feels like we'll be a cheerful team.

11:24.490 --> 11:27.490
From today on, with Tsubasa as the captain at our core,

11:27.490 --> 11:30.350
we'll show them how the new Nankatsu FC plays football.

11:30.350 --> 11:31.600
Yes, coach!

11:31.600 --> 11:33.990
Come and greet your teammates as the new captain.

11:33.990 --> 11:34.500
Yes, sir!

11:39.300 --> 11:41.970
Let's be the best in Japan!

11:41.970 --> 11:43.700
Yeah!

11:53.340 --> 11:56.310
Mom! They made me the captain!

11:56.310 --> 11:58.310
What? You?

11:58.310 --> 12:01.030
Yep. I need to tell Roberto, too!

12:01.030 --> 12:02.110
Where is he?

12:02.110 --> 12:04.370
I think he just went out.

12:04.370 --> 12:06.870
What? That sucks.

12:06.870 --> 12:11.750
You'll have to start doing better if you're gonna be the captain.

12:11.750 --> 12:13.000
Yeah!

12:19.750 --> 12:22.640
Why does my heart waver,

12:22.640 --> 12:25.510
when they are both okay with it?

12:25.510 --> 12:29.510
Wasn't I the one that said that I wanted to take Tsubasa to Brazil?

12:29.510 --> 12:32.770
Why am I still torn up?

12:35.770 --> 12:39.520
<i>It's the National Tournament now, Tsubasa.</i>

12:39.520 --> 12:41.140
<i>Do your best!</i>

12:41.140 --> 12:42.440
<i>And, I am counting on you</i>

12:42.440 --> 12:44.570
<i>for everything after that, Roberto.</i>

12:47.610 --> 12:50.910
<i>Finally, the day Nankatsu FC leaves for Tokyo</i>

12:50.910 --> 12:55.460
<i>to go where the Nationals are held has arrived!</i>

12:55.460 --> 12:59.360
Well then, as a prayer wishing for Nankatsu's victory,

12:59.360 --> 13:07.510
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

13:07.510 --> 13:09.510
What a send-off!

13:09.510 --> 13:11.460
This is basically just showing off!

13:11.460 --> 13:13.770
Your mom is amazing!

13:13.770 --> 13:16.020
Ryo! Kick their butts!

13:16.020 --> 13:19.040
Wakabayashi didn't come for the send-off.

13:19.890 --> 13:22.190
I'm sure he can't stand to watch us leave without him.

13:22.920 --> 13:25.940
<i>I'll make sure to keep your promise, Wakabayashi.</i>

13:25.940 --> 13:27.070
Tsubasa!

13:27.570 --> 13:30.850
<i>Roberto! Watch my matches!</i>

13:30.850 --> 13:33.770
<i>I'll make sure I'm going to Brazil!</i>

13:36.870 --> 13:40.840
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

13:41.960 --> 13:47.220
Tsubasa! We'll come by later!

13:52.560 --> 13:54.560
<i>Counting on you, everybody!</i>

13:55.240 --> 13:57.940
<i>I'll be there too!</i>

13:58.980 --> 14:00.940
— Tokyo —

14:00.940 --> 14:03.940
— Bay Coast Football Park —

14:07.470 --> 14:10.070
Finally, we're here, the Nationals!

14:10.070 --> 14:11.870
You're always energetic!

14:12.780 --> 14:14.610
Is everybody here?

14:14.610 --> 14:17.250
Make sure to check one last time, in case you missed anything!

14:17.250 --> 14:19.480
You wanna go check out the field?

14:19.480 --> 14:22.240
Let's get the bags to the hotel, first.

14:22.240 --> 14:24.920
Hey! What are you kids doing?!

14:27.010 --> 14:28.130
What?!

14:28.130 --> 14:29.630
Take that, Kazuo!

14:30.510 --> 14:31.510
Nice pass!

14:31.510 --> 14:32.150
What?

14:32.150 --> 14:34.650
What are those guys doing?

14:34.650 --> 14:38.180
They are passing the ball across to both sides of the platform.

14:38.850 --> 14:42.480
Hey! Stop it, you two!

14:42.480 --> 14:45.320
Tokyo station's officers sure are obnoxious!

14:48.050 --> 14:48.780
Masao!

14:49.240 --> 14:50.320
Nice pass!

14:52.320 --> 14:54.240
They're twins!

14:54.240 --> 14:55.400
Take that!

14:55.400 --> 14:56.290
Here!

14:56.290 --> 14:57.080
Take that!

14:57.080 --> 15:00.830
Masao, Kazuo, hurry up or we're leaving without you!

15:00.830 --> 15:02.020
Yeah!

15:02.020 --> 15:03.580
Kazuo, let's go!

15:03.580 --> 15:06.090
Hey, this is the last one! Take that!

15:06.400 --> 15:08.590
Okay! Huh?

15:09.120 --> 15:11.600
Are you guys in the National Tournament too?

15:11.600 --> 15:12.390
Yeah.

15:12.390 --> 15:15.970
We're Hanawa Youth Football Club, from Akita.

15:15.970 --> 15:17.140
We look forward to defeating you!

15:17.140 --> 15:19.040
Masao, hurry up!

15:19.040 --> 15:20.390
Yeah!

15:20.390 --> 15:21.970
What's with these guys?

15:21.970 --> 15:23.400
Weirdos, I guess.

15:23.400 --> 15:25.920
But, they were really nimble.

15:25.920 --> 15:27.650
Yeah, they sure were.

15:28.160 --> 15:29.240
<i>That's right.</i>

15:29.240 --> 15:32.910
<i>There are many other amazing players at the National tournament.</i>

15:33.530 --> 15:35.370
<i>We'd better keep that in mind when we play.</i>

15:37.580 --> 15:40.440
<i>The National Youth Football Tournament</i>

15:40.440 --> 15:43.500
<i>is a yearly tournament for youth footballers,</i>

15:43.500 --> 15:46.590
<i>held during summer vacation.</i>

15:46.590 --> 15:49.850
<i>48 teams from all over the country are</i>

15:49.850 --> 15:56.680
<i>put in blocks of six, and 2 of each block</i>

15:56.680 --> 16:00.980
<i>are pitted against each other for the championship.</i>

16:05.230 --> 16:06.360
Misaki!

16:06.360 --> 16:07.260
Huh?

16:07.260 --> 16:10.390
Oh! Matsuyama! You guys!

16:10.390 --> 16:12.260
It's you!

16:12.260 --> 16:15.640
Who would've thought you went to Nankatsu, one of the top contenders?

16:15.640 --> 16:18.370
These guys were my teammates, back in Hokkaido.

16:18.370 --> 16:19.580
Wow!

16:19.990 --> 16:21.450
I'm Matsuyama, the captain.

16:21.450 --> 16:24.670
He's our captain, Tsubasa Ozora.

16:24.670 --> 16:25.540
I'm looking forward to playing you.

16:25.540 --> 16:27.450
Nice to finally meet you.

16:27.450 --> 16:29.800
I heard a lot about you from Misaki.

16:31.210 --> 16:33.780
This time, we're opponents.

16:33.780 --> 16:35.510
Yeah, that's right!

16:35.510 --> 16:38.380
Wait, Tsubasa!

16:38.380 --> 16:39.060
Oh!

16:39.060 --> 16:40.770
Now it's Tsubasa.

16:41.110 --> 16:43.400
Glad I found you.

16:43.400 --> 16:47.770
Let me introduce our captain, Jun Misugi.

16:47.770 --> 16:50.900
Nice to meet you. I'm Misugi from Musashi FC.

16:51.440 --> 16:53.960
Tsubasa Ozora, nice to meet you too.

16:53.960 --> 16:56.780
I look forward to having a game with you.

16:57.160 --> 16:59.650
<i>She sure is cute!</i>

16:59.650 --> 17:02.600
Aren't you from Nankatsu FC?

17:02.600 --> 17:05.120
Woah! He's huge!

17:05.120 --> 17:07.880
Is it true that Wakabayashi ain't coming?

17:07.880 --> 17:10.040
Yeah, it's true.

17:10.040 --> 17:12.990
I'm Nakanishi from Naniwa FC.

17:12.990 --> 17:18.950
If Wakabayashi ain't here, then I'm the number one keeper here!

17:19.760 --> 17:20.430
Oh!

17:21.200 --> 17:23.260
<i>It's the guys from the station.</i>

17:23.260 --> 17:27.190
<i>Akita's Hanawa Youth Soccer Club, I think?</i>

17:28.440 --> 17:30.190
Kojiro Hyuga!

17:30.190 --> 17:31.940
Meiwa FC?

17:32.590 --> 17:36.190
<i>Tsubasa's rivals have all come together.</i>

17:40.990 --> 17:43.950
Now, we'll be drawing lots to determine the teams in each block.

17:43.950 --> 17:48.880
Tsubasa Ozora, captain of Nankatsu FC, representative of Shizuoka.

17:48.880 --> 17:49.710
Here!

17:53.930 --> 17:58.550
Nankatsu FC enters first into the first block as the A team!

17:59.390 --> 18:04.610
All right, Tsubasa! First block A team sounds very nice. Good pick!

18:08.850 --> 18:10.650
What is he doing?

18:10.650 --> 18:13.770
Meiwa FC enters the first block, as the B team!

18:14.810 --> 18:16.230
What?

18:16.230 --> 18:18.490
Then, our first game will be–

18:18.490 --> 18:20.490
Meiwa FC?

18:21.550 --> 18:22.900
Wakabayashi!

18:24.960 --> 18:27.040
Yeah. I heard the news just a few moments ago.

18:27.040 --> 18:33.170
Get better soon so we can play together in the finals.

18:33.170 --> 18:37.320
Yeah. Win, Tsubasa. Make sure of it!

18:37.320 --> 18:39.300
We'll win. I promise.

18:40.960 --> 18:43.550
I'm sure he's frustrated.

18:44.160 --> 18:47.560
Damn it! If this leg was okay, I'd—

18:48.510 --> 18:53.190
Why it had to be the first game?!

18:59.060 --> 19:02.780
Captain! You need to wear the captain band.

19:06.250 --> 19:07.490
You wear it.

19:07.490 --> 19:09.460
What, me?

19:09.460 --> 19:11.210
I don't want to wear it.

19:12.420 --> 19:14.210
Yes!

19:17.420 --> 19:20.050
Hey, stop! Stop!

19:23.770 --> 19:26.130
It's not looking good, boss.

19:26.130 --> 19:28.080
Everyone's stingy.

19:28.080 --> 19:30.560
If that's the case,

19:30.560 --> 19:33.200
you two go and get hit by a car.

19:33.200 --> 19:34.620
They'll stop then!

19:34.620 --> 19:36.580
That's cruel!

19:37.610 --> 19:44.200
{TS: Tokaido Express}

19:38.460 --> 19:40.170
Hey, young fellas!

19:40.170 --> 19:41.590
Want a lift?

19:41.590 --> 19:42.790
You mean it?

19:42.790 --> 19:44.200
Can you take us to Tokyo?

19:44.200 --> 19:45.140
Yeah!

19:45.140 --> 19:46.830
I'm going to Tokyo too!

19:46.830 --> 19:48.680
Hurry and get on!

19:48.680 --> 19:52.080
Everybody, we got lucky! It's a truck!

19:52.450 --> 19:53.300
Wow!

19:53.300 --> 19:53.910
We did it!

19:53.910 --> 19:55.420
We can all go cheer them!

19:55.420 --> 19:59.550
Wait, wait! I can't get you all in the truck, its against the rules.

19:59.550 --> 20:00.380
What?

20:00.380 --> 20:02.090
Let me handle it.

20:02.090 --> 20:05.340
We truck drivers can't leave the troubled behind.

20:05.340 --> 20:07.150
Calling for backup.

20:07.150 --> 20:08.460
I repeat, calling for backup.

20:08.460 --> 20:10.390
I'm calling from Nankatsu town in Shizuoka.

20:10.390 --> 20:13.070
Our luggage is a little miss and her friends.

20:13.070 --> 20:14.590
Counting on you!

20:20.610 --> 20:21.570
Wow!

20:21.570 --> 20:23.210
Awesome!

20:23.210 --> 20:25.110
Get on the other trucks too, guys.

20:28.910 --> 20:30.880
Can we get going, old man?

20:30.880 --> 20:32.750
What are you guys gonna do there?

20:32.750 --> 20:34.260
We're cheering for our football team!

20:34.260 --> 20:36.860
Oh! So you guys are the cheer squad!

20:36.860 --> 20:37.630
That's right!

20:37.630 --> 20:41.140
Is that so? I like football too.

20:41.140 --> 20:42.920
Huh? But, if you were a manager,

20:42.920 --> 20:46.840
wouldn't you have gone with the team?

20:47.720 --> 20:49.710
That's a taboo subject...!

20:50.670 --> 20:52.730
<i>We don't need a manager.</i>

20:52.730 --> 20:57.160
<i>Because of the coach, I wasn't able to become a manager.</i>

20:57.160 --> 21:02.310
But, I'm coming to cheer for you on, Tsubasa!

21:07.310 --> 21:09.200
<i>Participants, enter!</i>

21:09.200 --> 21:13.280
{TS: Furano Youth Football Club(above) Hokkaido(below)}

21:10.190 --> 21:14.460
<i>Here it is, the National Youth Football Tournament! This year as all others,</i>

21:15.000 --> 21:18.460
<i>from the north to the very south, 48 teams of young footballers</i>

21:18.460 --> 21:21.080
<i>have won their preliminary tournaments</i>

21:21.080 --> 21:25.220
<i>to engage in heated matches in this tournament.</i>

21:25.220 --> 21:28.390
<i>We are sure that a lot of these youngsters</i>

21:28.390 --> 21:31.490
<i>will showcase their abilities in this tournament.</i>

21:32.310 --> 21:35.480
{TS: Nankatsu FC(above) Shizuoka Prefecture(below)}

21:33.800 --> 21:36.560
It's about to begin. The National Tournament.

21:40.170 --> 21:41.780
<i>A pledge from the participant,</i>

21:41.780 --> 21:45.570
<i>captain of Nankatsu FC, Tsubasa Ozora.</i>

21:49.720 --> 21:55.080
I pledge! We participants, will act with sportsmanship and will compete

21:55.080 --> 21:58.810
while adhering to the tenets of fair play!

21:58.810 --> 22:04.090
I am the captain of Nankatsu FC, Tsubasa Ozora!

22:06.720 --> 22:09.370
Wow! He did well.

22:09.370 --> 22:11.370
Right, Roberto?

22:11.370 --> 22:12.510
Yes.

22:16.140 --> 22:18.760
<i>Sportsmanship?</i>

22:38.950 --> 22:44.830
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.950 --> 22:44.830
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.830 --> 22:50.840
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.830 --> 22:50.840
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.850
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.850
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:02.310
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:02.310
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.270 --> 23:08.440
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.270 --> 23:08.440
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.360 --> 23:15.160
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.360 --> 23:15.160
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.160 --> 23:21.200
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.200 --> 23:26.210
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.200 --> 23:26.210
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.500 --> 23:33.380
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.500 --> 23:33.380
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.380 --> 23:39.260
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.260 --> 23:46.150
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.260 --> 23:46.150
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.240 --> 24:00.810
COMING UP, EPISODE 14:
FIRE UP, NANKATSU! DEFEAT MEIWA!!
